IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `scja-core`

-- Supreme Court of Judicature Act 1969 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation in force from 1 July 2024.
-- The source is a plain-text rendering (SCJA1969.txt), not the official text. Layer 1: the law, objectively; every name begins with the label of its provision.
-- scja2-part4-ad-general.l4: Part 4 (Appellate Division), Division 1, General: ss 30 to 34 (President, jurisdiction, composition, decisions, sittings).
-- JUST TRUE and JUST FALSE are answers the Act gives in its own words; NOTHING means the Act does not answer on these facts (see NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING (scja2)").
-- Twin: ss 30-34 and ss 48-52 say the same thing about the two courts; each section is encoded on its own (ruling E1, option C) with the wording kept alike.

§ `Part 4, Division 1 -- General`

§§ `s 30 -- President`

-- src:2318 | 30.—(1) The Chief Justice may appoint a Judge of the Appellate
-- src:2319 | Division to be the President of the Appellate Division.
@ref s 30(1) (src:2318-2319)
GIVEN office IS A `Kind of Judge`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 30(1) the Chief Justice may appoint the Judge to be the President of the Appellate Division` MEANS
    IF office EQUALS `Judge of the Appellate Division`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is to appoint "a Judge of the Appellate Division"; the text does not say whether anyone else may be appointed
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2323 | (2) If no appointment is made under subsection (1), the Chief
-- src:2324 | Justice is the President of the Appellate Division.
@ref s 30(2) (src:2323-2324)
GIVEN `an appointment is made under section 30(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 30(2) the Chief Justice is the President of the Appellate Division` MEANS
    IF NOT `an appointment is made under section 30(1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If no appointment is made under subsection (1)" -- the "if" is not met when an appointment has been made, so this subsection does not make the Chief Justice the President
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:2330 | (a) the most senior Supreme Court Judge, as determined by
-- src:2331 | section 4, is to preside; and
@ref s 30(3)(a) (src:2330-2331)
GIVEN judge IS A Judge
      `s 4 the most senior Supreme Court Judge among those sitting` IS A MAYBE Judge
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 30(3)(a) the Judge is to preside in a sitting of the Appellate Division` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 4 the most senior Supreme Court Judge among those sitting`
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): who is the most senior Supreme Court Judge is determined by section 4, which another part of this encoding answers (PLAN.md seam 12)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST senior THEN
        IF senior's `reference for this person` EQUALS judge's `reference for this person`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the text names the most senior Supreme Court Judge as the one who presides and does not say anything of another Judge
        ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2338 | (b) if there is no Supreme Court Judge, the Chief Justice is to
-- src:2339 | appoint a person to preside.
@ref s 30(3)(b) (src:2338-2339)
GIVEN `there is a Supreme Court Judge sitting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 30(3)(b) the Chief Justice is to appoint a person to preside in a sitting of the Appellate Division` MEANS
    IF NOT `there is a Supreme Court Judge sitting`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if there is no Supreme Court Judge" -- the "if" is not met when a Supreme Court Judge is sitting
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `s 31 -- Jurisdiction, general`

-- src:2345 | 31.—(1) The Appellate Division has the civil jurisdiction
-- src:2346 | mentioned in section 35.
@ref s 31(1) (src:2345-2346)
GIVEN `s 35(2) the matter is one of the matters of the civil jurisdiction of the Appellate Division` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 31(1) the Appellate Division has the civil jurisdiction mentioned in section 35 over the matter` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 35(2) the matter is one of the matters of the civil jurisdiction of the Appellate Division`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection gives the jurisdiction "mentioned in section 35"; for a matter that section does not mention, or does not settle, this subsection says nothing
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): section 35(2) does not settle the matter
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- src:2350 | (2) The Appellate Division has no criminal jurisdiction.
@ref s 31(2) (src:2350)
GIVEN nature IS A `Nature of the proceeding`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 31(2) the Appellate Division has criminal jurisdiction over the proceeding` MEANS
    CONSIDER nature
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Appellate Division has no criminal jurisdiction."
    WHEN `a criminal proceeding` THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the text speaks of criminal jurisdiction and says nothing of a quasi-criminal proceeding (K4)
    WHEN `a quasi-criminal proceeding` THEN NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection says what the Appellate Division lacks, criminal jurisdiction; it is silent on a civil proceeding
    WHEN `a civil proceeding` THEN NOTHING

-- src:2354 | (3) The Appellate Division has, in an appeal and for any purpose
-- src:2355 | relating to an appeal, all the jurisdiction and powers of the court or
-- src:2356 | tribunal from which the appeal was brought.
@ref s 31(3) (src:2354-2356)
GIVEN `it is an appeal, or a purpose relating to an appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the power is one that the court or tribunal from which the appeal was brought has` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 31(3) the Appellate Division has the jurisdiction or power of the court or tribunal from which the appeal was brought` MEANS
    IF `it is an appeal, or a purpose relating to an appeal` AND `the power is one that the court or tribunal from which the appeal was brought has`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant is "in an appeal and for any purpose relating to an appeal" and of the jurisdiction and powers of the court or tribunal appealed from
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2360 | (4) The Appellate Division may decide any question that needs to
-- src:2361 | be decided to do justice in any case before it.
@ref s 31(4) (src:2360-2361)
GIVEN `the question needs to be decided to do justice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the question arises in a case before the Appellate Division` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 31(4) the Appellate Division may decide the question` MEANS
    IF `the question needs to be decided to do justice` AND `the question arises in a case before the Appellate Division`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant is of "any question that needs to be decided to do justice in any case before it"
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 32 -- Composition, general`

-- src:2367 | 32.—(1) Subject to this Act, the jurisdiction of the Appellate
-- src:2368 | Division is to be exercised by 3 or any greater uneven number of
-- src:2369 | Judges.
@ref s 32(1) (src:2367-2369)
GIVEN `the number of Judges who exercise the jurisdiction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 32(1) the number of Judges is one that the subsection provides for` MEANS
    IF `the number of Judges who exercise the jurisdiction` AT LEAST 3 AND (`the number of Judges who exercise the jurisdiction` MODULO 2) EQUALS 1
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subject to this Act" -- other provisions of the Act allow other numbers (ss 36(1), 40(3) and (4)), and the subsection does not say in terms that another number is invalid
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2373 | (2) A Judge must not sit in the Appellate Division to hear or decide
-- src:2374 | any appeal from a decision made by the Judge, or any matter related
-- src:2375 | to such an appeal.
@ref s 32(2) (src:2373-2375)
GIVEN `the matter is an appeal from a decision made by the Judge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter is related to such an appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 32(2) the Judge may sit in the Appellate Division to hear or decide the matter` MEANS
    IF `the matter is an appeal from a decision made by the Judge` OR `the matter is related to such an appeal`
    THEN
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A Judge must not sit in the Appellate Division to hear or decide any appeal from a decision made by the Judge, or any matter related to such an appeal."
        JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the prohibition reaches only an appeal from the Judge's own decision and matters related to it; the subsection is silent on any other matter
    ELSE NOTHING

-- The prohibition is derived from the answer above (ruling N2): the text names its bearer, "A Judge".
DECLARE `s 32(2) party` IS ONE OF `s 32(2) the Judge who made the decision appealed from`
DECLARE `s 32(2) act` IS ONE OF `s 32(2) sits in the Appellate Division to hear or decide the appeal`

-- src:2373 | (2) A Judge must not sit in the Appellate Division to hear or decide
-- src:2374 | any appeal from a decision made by the Judge, or any matter related
-- src:2375 | to such an appeal.
@ref s 32(2) (src:2373-2375)
`s 32(2) the prohibition on the Judge` MEANS
    PARTY `s 32(2) the Judge who made the decision appealed from`
    SHANT `s 32(2) sits in the Appellate Division to hear or decide the appeal`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 32(2) the Judge who made the decision appealed from` BECAUSE "a Judge sat in the Appellate Division to hear or decide an appeal from the Judge's own decision"

#TRACE `s 32(2) the prohibition on the Judge` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 32(2) the Judge who made the decision appealed from` DOES `s 32(2) sits in the Appellate Division to hear or decide the appeal` AT 1

-- src:2379 | (3) Section 10A applies in relation to proceedings before the
-- src:2380 | Appellate Division as it applies in relation to proceedings before the
-- src:2381 | General Division.
@ref s 32(3) (src:2379-2381)
GIVEN `s 10A the court may summon assessors` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 32(3) the Appellate Division may summon assessors as section 10A allows` MEANS
    -- section 10A "applies in relation to proceedings before the Appellate Division as it applies in relation to proceedings before the General Division": the answer is the one section 10A gives for this court (PLAN.md seam 13), passed through unchanged
    `s 10A the court may summon assessors`

§§ `s 33 -- Decisions how made`

-- src:2387 | 33.—(1) A decision of the Appellate Division is to be made in
-- src:2388 | accordance with the opinion of the majority of the Judges hearing the
-- src:2389 | case.
@ref s 33(1) (src:2387-2389)
GIVEN `how the Judges divided` IS A `Split of opinion`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 33(1) the decision goes the way of the opinion of the majority of the Judges hearing the case` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- the answer is JUST TRUE where the majority are for the claim, appeal or application
        IF `how the Judges divided`'s `Judges for the claim, appeal or application` GREATER THAN `how the Judges divided`'s `Judges against it` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in accordance with the opinion of the majority" -- the decision follows a majority against the claim, appeal or application
        IF `how the Judges divided`'s `Judges for the claim, appeal or application` LESS THAN `how the Judges divided`'s `Judges against it` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): an even division has no majority; subsection (2) deals with an appeal or application
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:2398 | (2) An appeal or application to the Appellate Division is to be
-- src:2399 | dismissed if the Judges hearing the appeal or application are evenly
-- src:2400 | divided.
@ref s 33(2) (src:2398-2400)
GIVEN `how the Judges divided` IS A `Split of opinion`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 33(2) the appeal or application is dismissed because the Judges hearing it are evenly divided` MEANS
    IF `how the Judges divided`'s `Judges for the claim, appeal or application` EQUALS `how the Judges divided`'s `Judges against it`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the Judges hearing the appeal or application are evenly divided" -- the "if" is not met
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `s 34 -- Sittings`

-- src:2408 | (a) is to sit on such dates and at such places as the Chief Justice
-- src:2409 | may from time to time appoint; and
@ref s 34(1)(a) (src:2408-2409)
GIVEN `the Chief Justice has appointed the date` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 34(1)(a) the date is one that the Chief Justice appointed` MEANS
    IF `the Chief Justice has appointed the date`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the Appellate Division "is to sit on such dates ... as the Chief Justice may from time to time appoint"; the text does not say that a sitting on another date is invalid
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2408 | (a) is to sit on such dates and at such places as the Chief Justice
-- src:2409 | may from time to time appoint; and
@ref s 34(1)(a) (src:2408-2409)
GIVEN `the Chief Justice has appointed the place` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 34(1)(a) the place is one that the Chief Justice appointed` MEANS
    IF `the Chief Justice has appointed the place`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the Appellate Division "is to sit ... at such places as the Chief Justice may from time to time appoint"; the text does not say that a sitting at another place is invalid
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2411 | (b) may sit on a Saturday, Sunday or public holiday, or during
-- src:2412 | a vacation, if the Chief Justice so appoints.
@ref s 34(1)(b) (src:2411-2412)
GIVEN `the day is a Saturday, Sunday or public holiday, or falls during a vacation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Chief Justice so appoints` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 34(1)(b) the Appellate Division may sit on the day` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph speaks only of a Saturday, Sunday or public holiday, or a vacation
        IF NOT `the day is a Saturday, Sunday or public holiday, or falls during a vacation` THEN NOTHING
        IF `the Chief Justice so appoints` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the Chief Justice so appoints" -- the "if" is not met
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:2416 | (2) The Chief Justice may cancel or postpone a sitting appointed
-- src:2417 | under subsection (1).
@ref s 34(2) (src:2416-2417)
GIVEN `the sitting was appointed under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 34(2) the Chief Justice may cancel or postpone the sitting` MEANS
    IF `the sitting was appointed under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is over "a sitting appointed under subsection (1)"
    ELSE NOTHING
